{"text": "\u2018Canada's Expert Committee on Cigarette Modification\n\nBill Rickert, Ph.D., Chair\n\u2018Canada's Expert Committee on Cigarette Modification,\n\u2018co Labstat Incorporated,\n262 Manitou Drive,\nKitchener, Ontario,\nN2C1L3\n\nIuly 31, 1996\n\nDr. David Townsend, Senior Principal Scientist,\nRJ, Reynolds Tobacco Company,\n\u2018Bowman Gray Technical Center,\nP.O. Box 1487,\nWinston-Salem, NC, 27102-1487,\nUSA.\n\nDear David:\n\n\u2018The process of producing the \u201cfinal\u201d draf of the report of Canada's Expert Committee on Cigarette\n\u2018Modification bas taken somewhat longes than anticipated. However the process is now complete and'1\n1hope (optimistically?) that the enclosed draft will become the final report. Recognizing that there are\ndifferences of opinion among committee members, I decided to adhere, as closely as possible, tothe\n\u2018wrtien transcript ofthe meetings in order to avoid controversy. Inthe final analysis, this i a weaknesses\n\u2018of the report in that, because of difficulties in reaching a consensus (and the lack of time), there is itl in\nthe report in the way of specific recommendations. However, Ido feel thatthe document contains an\nabundance of important and useful information which will be valuable resource for the Canadian\nGovernment as it considers its legislative agenda with respect to tobacco.\n\nIn reviewing this final draft, 1 would ask that you read the document ensuring that I have made the\n\u2018changes which you have suggested. Requests for additional changes should be limited gly to errors or\n\u2018omissions in regard to the information which you submitted in response to the second draft. However, if\n\u2018there are grammatical or spelling errors which have escaped notice, please bring these to my attention as\nwell\n\n[Ifyou can accept the document as written, I would ask you sign page 92 and fax the copy back to me: I\n\u2018will then scan in your signature along with those ofthe other members and reinsert the page. At this\npint the document becomes the offical report of the committee and will be submitted as such to the\nOffice of Tobacco Control. ~\n\n\u2018Thank you, once again, for your participation in an extremely important process and I ook forward to\n\u2018having to opportunity of working with you on other occasions.\n\n\u2018Yours sincerely\nBaw Ridbooe\n\nWS. Gill) Ricken, Chair\nenc\n\n\u2018Sponsored by Health Canada\n\n99T9 vs9Ts", "words": [{"text": "\u2018Canada's", "x0": 196, "y0": 8, "x1": 243, "y1": 18, "conf": 72.0}, {"text": "Expert", "x0": 246, "y0": 8, "x1": 278, "y1": 20, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "Committee", "x0": 281, "y0": 8, "x1": 333, "y1": 18, "conf": 18.0}, {"text": "on", "x0": 336, "y0": 11, "x1": 348, "y1": 18, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "Cigarette", "x0": 352, "y0": 8, "x1": 397, "y1": 21, "conf": 73.0}, {"text": "Modification", "x0": 400, "y0": 9, "x1": 463, "y1": 21, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "Bill", "x0": 83, "y0": 101, "x1": 100, "y1": 110, "conf": 76.0}, {"text": "Rickert,", "x0": 104, "y0": 101, "x1": 142, "y1": 112, "conf": 79.0}, {"text": "Ph.D.,", "x0": 145, "y0": 102, "x1": 176, "y1": 112, "conf": 40.0}, {"text": "Chair", "x0": 180, "y0": 102, "x1": 208, "y1": 111, "conf": 90.0}, {"text": "\u2018Canada's", "x0": 83, "y0": 115, "x1": 128, "y1": 125, "conf": 86.0}, {"text": "Expert", "x0": 131, "y0": 116, "x1": 163, "y1": 127, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "Committee", "x0": 167, "y0": 116, "x1": 220, "y1": 126, "conf": 93.0}, {"text": "on", "x0": 223, "y0": 119, "x1": 235, "y1": 126, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "Cigarette", "x0": 239, "y0": 116, "x1": 282, "y1": 129, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "Modification,", "x0": 286, "y0": 117, "x1": 350, "y1": 128, "conf": 68.0}, {"text": "\u2018co", "x0": 82, "y0": 129, "x1": 97, "y1": 139, "conf": 43.0}, {"text": "Labstat", "x0": 100, "y0": 129, "x1": 135, "y1": 140, "conf": 63.0}, {"text": "Incorporated,", "x0": 138, "y0": 130, "x1": 203, "y1": 142, "conf": 93.0}, {"text": "262", "x0": 83, 